+## String instructions as named pcodeops (T21c, #97 B4). The T17 p-code loops were exact but decompiled as loops;
+## the decompiler now shows one call per instruction. Register and flag effects follow the RXv2 software manual
+## R01US0071EJ0100 (SCMPU p. 184, SMOVB p. 189, SMOVF p. 190, SMOVU p. 191, SSTR p. 192, SUNTIL p. 196, SWHILE p. 198):
+##   scmpu(R1, R2, R3)        returns *R1 - *R2 (unsigned bytes, zero-extended) of the last compared pair: 0 when the
+##                            strings matched (Z), >= 0 when C is set. R1/R2 are undefined afterwards (left unchanged).
+##   smovf/smovb(R1, R2, R3)  copies R3 bytes from R2 to R1; R1/R2 end one past (before) the last byte, R3 = 0.
+##   smovu(R1, R2, R3)        copies up to R3 bytes up to and including NUL; returns the new R3. R1/R2 undefined (unchanged).
+##   sstr(R1, R2:size, R3)    stores R2 (.B/.W/.L) R3 times at R1; R1 ends one element past the last store, R3 = 0.
+##   suntil/swhile(R1, R2, R3, size)  returns the new R1 (one element past the last compared one); R3 is reduced by the
+##                            number of compares, Z/C come from that last element - R2 (unsigned).
+## Every instruction is a no-op when R3 = 0 (manual), so the call is skipped then.
+define pcodeop scmpu;
+define pcodeop smovf;
+define pcodeop smovb;
+define pcodeop smovu;
+define pcodeop sstr;
+define pcodeop suntil;
+define pcodeop swhile;
+
